From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] installd compiles everything when the profile a filter asks for is missing

A compiler filter that compiles from a usage profile, with no profile to compile
from, compiles nothing at all: "If we are using a profile filter but do not have
a profile compilation info, compile nothing" (art/compiler/driver/
compiler_driver.cc). Nothing is a working answer on a phone, where the
interpreter and the JIT catch up in a few seconds. Here it is not: WeRead with
no compiled code takes over two minutes to reach its bookshelf and shows "isn't
responding" (Test V32).

A new flag, DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE, lets the caller say which of the two it
would rather have. installd is where the question can be answered: the profile
belongs to the application's own user and group, and the system server cannot
read it. When the flag is set and there is no reference profile with anything in
it, the compilation is done with "speed" instead, and profile_guided is dropped
with it so that no application image is written from the classes of a profile
that is not there.

The caller that sets it is the recompilation after a system update
(PackageManagerService.performDexOptUpgrade, frameworks/base patch 0047).

diff --git a/cmds/installd/installd_constants.h b/cmds/installd/installd_constants.h
--- a/cmds/installd/installd_constants.h
+++ b/cmds/installd/installd_constants.h
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@
 constexpr int DEXOPT_FORCE          = 1 << 6;
 constexpr int DEXOPT_STORAGE_CE     = 1 << 7;
 constexpr int DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE     = 1 << 8;
+// PW3: compile with "speed" when the filter asks for a usage profile and there is
+// no profile to compile from. Set for the recompilation after a system update,
+// where the alternative is an application left with no compiled code; see dexopt().
+constexpr int DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE = 1 << 9;
 
 /* all known values for dexopt flags */
 constexpr int DEXOPT_MASK =
@@ -59,7 +63,8 @@
     | DEXOPT_SECONDARY_DEX
     | DEXOPT_FORCE
     | DEXOPT_STORAGE_CE
-    | DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE;
+    | DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE
+    | DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE;
 
 // NOTE: keep in sync with StorageManager
 constexpr int FLAG_STORAGE_DE = 1 << 0;
diff --git a/cmds/installd/otapreopt.cpp b/cmds/installd/otapreopt.cpp
--- a/cmds/installd/otapreopt.cpp
+++ b/cmds/installd/otapreopt.cpp
@@ -78,8 +78,13 @@
 static_assert(DEXOPT_FORCE          == 1 << 6, "DEXOPT_FORCE unexpected.");
 static_assert(DEXOPT_STORAGE_CE     == 1 << 7, "DEXOPT_STORAGE_CE unexpected.");
 static_assert(DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE     == 1 << 8, "DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE unexpected.");
+// PW3: the parameter protocol above is not what carries this flag. It is set by
+// PackageDexOptimizer for the recompilation after a system update, which runs in
+// installd; OtaDexoptService, the only writer of these parameters, never sets it.
+static_assert(DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE == 1 << 9,
+              "DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE unexpected.");
 
-static_assert(DEXOPT_MASK           == 0x1fe, "DEXOPT_MASK unexpected.");
+static_assert(DEXOPT_MASK           == 0x3fe, "DEXOPT_MASK unexpected.");
 
 
 
diff --git a/cmds/installd/dexopt.cpp b/cmds/installd/dexopt.cpp
--- a/cmds/installd/dexopt.cpp
+++ b/cmds/installd/dexopt.cpp
@@ -1213,6 +1213,15 @@
     return swap_fd;
 }
 
+// PW3: whether there is a reference profile with something in it to compile from.
+static bool reference_profile_exists(const std::string& pkgname, const std::string& dex_path,
+        bool is_secondary_dex) {
+    const std::string location = is_secondary_dex ? dex_path : pkgname;
+    struct stat st;
+    return stat(create_reference_profile_path(location, is_secondary_dex).c_str(), &st) == 0
+            && st.st_size > 0;
+}
+
 // Opens the reference profiles if needed.
 // Note that the reference profile might not exist so it's OK if the fd will be -1.
 Dex2oatFileWrapper maybe_open_reference_profile(const std::string& pkgname,
@@ -1625,6 +1634,20 @@
         CHECK((dexopt_flags & DEXOPT_STORAGE_DE) == 0);
     }
 
+    // PW3: a filter that compiles from a usage profile, with no profile to compile
+    // from, compiles nothing at all ("If we are using a profile filter but do not
+    // have a profile compilation info, compile nothing", compiler_driver.cc), and an
+    // application with no compiled code is unusable on this CPU: WeRead takes over
+    // two minutes to reach its bookshelf and shows "isn't responding" (Test V32).
+    // The caller sets this flag where compiling everything is the better of the two.
+    if (profile_guided && (dexopt_flags & DEXOPT_SPEED_IF_NO_PROFILE) != 0
